1
00:00:01,635 --> 00:00:02,636
Wow, the weather

2
00:00:02,703 --> 00:00:03,737
EPISODE 15

3
00:00:03,804 --> 00:00:06,773
is just amazing today,
truly amazing. Right, Min-gi?

4
00:00:07,474 --> 00:00:08,709
Huh?

5
00:00:09,376 --> 00:00:11,578
Right, it is.

6
00:00:11,645 --> 00:00:13,647
Yu-na, how about just us women later?

7
00:00:13,714 --> 00:00:16,283
-Shall we have some rice wine?
-Sure, why not?

8
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:19,319
Great! I can really hold my liquor.

9
00:00:19,386 --> 00:00:22,089
You'll really have to brace yourself.

10
00:00:22,155 --> 00:00:25,392
And how pathetic that punk used to be…

11
00:00:25,459 --> 00:00:27,194
I'll tell you all about it.

12
00:00:29,763 --> 00:00:32,699
Park Hong-gu, repeat three times:
"I'm dead meat today!"

13
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:35,402
We have piles and piles of work today!

14
00:00:35,469 --> 00:00:37,671
I get it, so stop scaring me.

15
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:39,172
Sure, work hard, guys.

16
00:00:39,239 --> 00:00:41,074
Yes, don't work too hard.

17
00:00:41,141 --> 00:00:43,410
-Take care.

18
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,980
Did you chicken out?

19
00:00:47,848 --> 00:00:51,184
Hey, doesn't she seem a bit weird?

20
00:00:51,251 --> 00:00:53,020
How so? She just looks happy.

21
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:54,488
It's nice she's cheerful.

22
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:56,857
No, she's definitely acting weird.

23
00:00:56,924 --> 00:00:59,927
You're weirder, you punk. You are.

24
00:00:59,993 --> 00:01:01,728
Let's just go catch snails.

25
00:01:01,795 --> 00:01:03,196
Yu-na is really pretty.

26
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:05,165
Oh, you silly kid.

27
00:01:14,107 --> 00:01:17,911
Wow, Hong-gu, it's been a while
since I did some shoveling with you.

28
00:01:17,978 --> 00:01:19,746
Hong-gu, is your shoveling better?

29
00:01:20,614 --> 00:01:22,516
It's no joke.

30
00:01:22,583 --> 00:01:24,051
I'm even ready for the army.

31
00:01:24,117 --> 00:01:27,988
Since it's been a while,
I'm going to give you a real test.

32
00:01:28,055 --> 00:01:29,890
-Got that?
-I'll show you later.

33
00:01:29,957 --> 00:01:32,559
Brace yourself, you rascal. Honestly.

34
00:01:49,009 --> 00:01:50,911
-You need more strength.
-Yun-hui!

35
00:01:55,716 --> 00:01:57,417
It's been a while, Yun-hui.

36
00:01:59,586 --> 00:02:02,189
Is that man by any chance…

37
00:02:02,255 --> 00:02:03,991
Hong-gu, go wait at home.

38
00:02:04,057 --> 00:02:05,993
-But…
-Go now!

39
00:02:23,176 --> 00:02:25,245
The air is nice here.

40
00:02:27,114 --> 00:02:30,017
Were you surprised I just showed up?

41
00:02:30,083 --> 00:02:32,719
No, just a little.

42
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,656
I saw on the news that you were back.

43
00:02:35,722 --> 00:02:38,392
You're a big success. Congratulations.

44
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,395
I wouldn't call it success.

45
00:02:41,461 --> 00:02:43,130
Have you been doing well?

46
00:02:43,196 --> 00:02:47,034
I've been busy just making ends meet.

47
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,469
Farming is so much work, you know.

48
00:02:49,536 --> 00:02:53,407
So you've stayed here ever since then?

49
00:02:53,473 --> 00:02:56,143
Turns out farming really suits me.

50
00:02:56,209 --> 00:02:58,078
Believe it or not, I'm Village Head.

51
00:02:58,145 --> 00:03:00,080
Village Head? You?

52
00:03:00,147 --> 00:03:03,684
That's right. Don't I look cool?

53
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:06,319
You've really changed a lot.

54
00:03:09,056 --> 00:03:11,091
So, what about marriage?

55
00:03:11,158 --> 00:03:12,592
Did you get married?

56
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,995
Not yet.

57
00:03:15,062 --> 00:03:17,397
I've been so busy farming,

58
00:03:17,464 --> 00:03:19,599
I haven't had time to get married.

59
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:22,669
What about you?

60
00:03:22,736 --> 00:03:24,938
Not yet for me, either.

61
00:03:26,273 --> 00:03:27,607
Really?

62
00:03:27,674 --> 00:03:30,077
Oh my, such a successful, handsome guy

63
00:03:30,143 --> 00:03:31,978
still hasn't been snatched up?

64
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:35,015
Women must be blind. Totally blind.

65
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:39,519
Anyway, has it been
eight years since we last met?

66
00:03:40,854 --> 00:03:43,523
Has it really been that long already?

67
00:03:44,357 --> 00:03:46,593
Time really flies.

68
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,696
I often wondered

69
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:55,035
what it would've been like
if I'd left with you back then.

70
00:03:57,971 --> 00:04:01,675
What do you think?
We would've just fought every day.

71
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:05,378
Besides, I'm bad at English
and had no talent for piano.

72
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:09,549
I think I'm just cut out for farming.

73
00:04:14,221 --> 00:04:16,823
Gosh, it's so late already.

74
00:04:16,890 --> 00:04:18,358
I have to go feed the cows.

75
00:04:18,425 --> 00:04:20,527
I should really get going.

76
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:22,329
All right.

77
00:04:22,395 --> 00:04:23,663
Oh, wait a second.

78
00:04:25,365 --> 00:04:29,469
This is a ticket to my recital.
Be sure to come if you have time.

79
00:04:32,172 --> 00:04:34,775
Oh my, you're at a great venue, too.

80
00:04:34,841 --> 00:04:35,976
LEE PIANO RECITAL

81
00:04:36,843 --> 00:04:39,579
But, um, I've been a bit busy lately.

82
00:04:39,646 --> 00:04:42,582
I'm not sure I can go, but I'll try.

83
00:04:43,350 --> 00:04:44,384
Okay.

84
00:04:44,451 --> 00:04:46,753
You have a long way to go. Get going.

85
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,855
-I'll head out, then.
-All right.

86
00:04:50,056 --> 00:04:52,058
-See you again.
-Sure.

87
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,369
Bye, and good luck with your recital!

88
00:05:58,859 --> 00:06:00,760
Here, please have some corn.

89
00:06:00,827 --> 00:06:02,329
Wow, that looks delicious!

90
00:06:03,263 --> 00:06:05,832
-Be careful, it's hot. Here.
-Ow, it's hot!

91
00:06:07,934 --> 00:06:09,169
Hello, I'm home.

92
00:06:09,236 --> 00:06:11,338
-Oh, welcome home.
-Welcome back.

93
00:06:11,404 --> 00:06:15,208
Oh, it's corn! Great, I was hungry.

94
00:06:15,275 --> 00:06:16,910
Thank you so much.

95
00:06:16,977 --> 00:06:18,144
It's delicious.

96
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:20,080
Goodness, it's steamed so well.

97
00:06:20,146 --> 00:06:22,682
-And where is Min-ho?
-He fell asleep earlier.

98
00:06:22,749 --> 00:06:25,285
My, the little guy must've been tired.

99
00:06:25,352 --> 00:06:28,455
Still, this is really steamed well.
It's delicious.

100
00:06:29,589 --> 00:06:32,659
Yun-hui, what did that man say?

101
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:34,928
What do you mean, "that man"?

102
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:37,764
No, it's really nothing.

103
00:06:37,831 --> 00:06:39,766
How is it nothing?

104
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:43,436
-That man is Min-ho's dad!
-What?

105
00:06:44,437 --> 00:06:45,438
Min-ho's dad?

106
00:06:45,505 --> 00:06:46,907
Park Hong-gu!

107
00:06:46,973 --> 00:06:49,376
What does that mean? Min-ho's dad?

108
00:06:50,043 --> 00:06:52,045
No, um, the thing is…

109
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,985
I mean, um…

110
00:06:59,052 --> 00:07:01,788
we weren't trying to eavesdrop…

111
00:07:02,622 --> 00:07:05,725
Yun-hui, I need a word with you.

112
00:07:16,169 --> 00:07:20,173
You should've told us
if something like that happened.

113
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:23,410
I'm sorry. I didn't want to worry you.

114
00:07:23,476 --> 00:07:25,979
Why did Min-ho's dad suddenly show up?

115
00:07:26,046 --> 00:07:27,247
What did he say?

116
00:07:27,914 --> 00:07:29,382
He didn't say much.

117
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:33,620
And he doesn't know Min-ho exists.

118
00:07:34,487 --> 00:07:35,755
What?

119
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:40,026
I found out after he left
that I was pregnant with Min-ho.

120
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:44,898
Then shouldn't you tell him now?

121
00:07:45,932 --> 00:07:49,402
He's doing so well.
I don't want to hold him back now.

122
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:51,404
I'm not saying to hold him back.

123
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,907
Shouldn't Min-ho know who his dad is

124
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:57,277
and where and how he's living?

125
00:07:57,944 --> 00:07:59,713
Min-ho is growing up so well,

126
00:07:59,779 --> 00:08:03,116
and I don't want to confuse him now.

127
00:08:03,183 --> 00:08:07,354
So please just trust me
and pretend you don't know.

128
00:08:08,188 --> 00:08:11,825
I've done fine on my own, haven't I?

129
00:08:14,294 --> 00:08:15,929
Oh, dear.

130
00:08:21,034 --> 00:08:23,970
So he doesn't even know Min-ho exists?

131
00:08:25,972 --> 00:08:27,574
It's all my fault.

132
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:31,111
If it weren't for me,
my sister wouldn't live like this.

133
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:33,847
Park Hong-gu, what are you saying?

134
00:08:33,913 --> 00:08:36,950
Stop talking nonsense.
Go inside and go to sleep.

135
00:08:38,284 --> 00:08:40,086
Are you okay?

136
00:08:40,153 --> 00:08:42,022
Of course I'm okay. Why?

137
00:08:42,088 --> 00:08:45,091
It's no big deal.
Why are you all making such a fuss?

138
00:08:45,158 --> 00:08:47,293
Go inside and get some rest, you all.

139
00:10:19,853 --> 00:10:21,888
Don't cry.

140
00:10:23,423 --> 00:10:25,692
I won't cry, Hong-gu.

141
00:10:43,343 --> 00:10:44,911
I came here one last time

142
00:10:45,712 --> 00:10:47,347
to ask you something.

143
00:10:47,947 --> 00:10:49,682
Come with me.

144
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:54,320
You know what a great chance this is.

145
00:10:54,387 --> 00:10:56,489
It's a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

146
00:10:56,556 --> 00:10:59,159
I told you, I can't go.

147
00:10:59,225 --> 00:11:01,928
Are you really giving up
on studying abroad?

148
00:11:02,762 --> 00:11:04,664
What can you do in the countryside?

149
00:11:04,731 --> 00:11:07,467
You'll farm after playing piano
all your life?

150
00:11:08,134 --> 00:11:11,938
-You'll throw away all your hard work?
-Then what about Hong-gu?

151
00:11:12,772 --> 00:11:16,176
You know I'm the only one left
to take care of Hong-gu.

152
00:11:16,242 --> 00:11:19,579
We can hire someone. I'll pay for it.

153
00:11:19,646 --> 00:11:22,282
You know it's not about that.

154
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:25,084
How can I leave
a grade-school kid all alone?

155
00:11:25,151 --> 00:11:26,819
He's not even your real brother.

156
00:11:26,886 --> 00:11:28,588
You don't share a drop of blood.

157
00:11:28,655 --> 00:11:32,292
But is he important enough to give up

158
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,860
your dreams and whole life?

159
00:11:35,161 --> 00:11:36,596
No.

160
00:11:37,964 --> 00:11:39,666
Is he more important than me?

161
00:11:43,169 --> 00:11:45,071
So let's go together.

162
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:48,041
I can't leave you here all alone.

163
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:06,125
I'm sorry, Hyeon-seok.

164
00:12:31,751 --> 00:12:32,852
Yun-hui.

165
00:12:42,562 --> 00:12:44,430
Don't worry, Hong-gu.

166
00:12:44,497 --> 00:12:47,233
I'll never go and leave you alone.

167
00:12:48,034 --> 00:12:50,536
I really won't leave you by yourself.

168
00:13:37,517 --> 00:13:40,353
Here, a strong Americano.

169
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:42,055
Thanks.

170
00:13:46,192 --> 00:13:48,895
But Yun-hui's had such a rough life.

171
00:13:48,961 --> 00:13:51,898
I know. If that hadn't happened,

172
00:13:51,964 --> 00:13:55,034
she could've been
a big-time pianist by now.

173
00:13:55,101 --> 00:13:56,736
-Don't you think?
-Right.

174
00:13:56,803 --> 00:14:00,206
And now someone like her
is the Village Head in the country.

175
00:14:00,273 --> 00:14:02,375
You never know how life turns out.

176
00:14:02,442 --> 00:14:04,110
-I know.
-Any one of us four

177
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:06,145
could die anytime, so let's live hard.

178
00:14:22,228 --> 00:14:24,397
Hey, do you think Yun-hui's okay?

179
00:14:24,464 --> 00:14:27,834
No way she's okay.
How could she not be torn up inside?

180
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:31,170
So let's really walk on eggshells
around her for now, okay?

181
00:14:31,237 --> 00:14:32,605
Hey, what are you doing?

182
00:14:33,639 --> 00:14:36,309
Hey, hurry to the village hall!
Fall in, fall in!

183
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:38,177
What?

184
00:14:40,847 --> 00:14:43,549
Why are you standing there
staring at me like that?

185
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:45,551
I'll go bring the village elders.

186
00:14:45,618 --> 00:14:49,021
Hurry over to the village hall,
okay? Off I go!

187
00:14:52,825 --> 00:14:54,260
She's totally hyped up.

188
00:14:54,327 --> 00:14:57,029
Right. Of all the times I've seen her,

189
00:14:57,096 --> 00:15:00,166
she looks the happiest today.

190
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:03,436
What is this? I feel like
such a fool for worrying.

191
00:15:03,503 --> 00:15:04,637
Why do I feel lousy?

192
00:15:04,704 --> 00:15:06,205
Is she doing it on purpose?

193
00:15:06,272 --> 00:15:08,207
Jeez.

194
00:15:10,877 --> 00:15:13,846
Gosh, what's this?
Shoulder pads, man? Shoulder pads?

195
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,948
It just gets like this on a hanger.

196
00:15:16,015 --> 00:15:16,983
What can I do?

197
00:15:17,049 --> 00:15:19,318
It's so obvious you're a bachelor.

198
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:20,987
Why'd you call us here again?

199
00:15:21,053 --> 00:15:23,256
Please hurry and take a seat.

200
00:15:23,322 --> 00:15:26,626
Now that the harvest is done,
you've all been bored, right?

201
00:15:26,692 --> 00:15:28,995
Still, we can't spend the whole winter

202
00:15:29,061 --> 00:15:31,798
drinking rice wine
and playing Go-Stop, can we?

203
00:15:31,864 --> 00:15:33,866
What can we do when there's no work?

204
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:37,303
So in my spare time, I wondered

205
00:15:37,370 --> 00:15:40,006
how we could make money even in winter,

206
00:15:40,072 --> 00:15:42,141
and I've been brainstorming ideas.

207
00:15:42,208 --> 00:15:45,478
Then one day, a great idea flashed

208
00:15:45,545 --> 00:15:47,713
through my mind like lightning.

209
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,315
And what might that be?

210
00:15:49,382 --> 00:15:52,151
I call it "Rural Experience Village."

211
00:15:52,218 --> 00:15:53,419
What do you think?

212
00:15:53,486 --> 00:15:55,388
A Rural Experience Village?

213
00:15:55,455 --> 00:15:57,957
Yes, even people in Seoul have taken

214
00:15:58,024 --> 00:16:00,026
more interest in rural life lately.

215
00:16:00,092 --> 00:16:02,995
So we offer those people experiences

216
00:16:03,062 --> 00:16:04,897
they can only get in the country.

217
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:07,500
What experiences?
What's to do in the country?

218
00:16:07,567 --> 00:16:09,836
Who says there's nothing to do?

219
00:16:09,902 --> 00:16:12,338
Greenhouse strawberry picking,
making kimchi,

220
00:16:12,405 --> 00:16:15,942
flying kites, puffed beans,
swinging fire cans, and plenty more.

221
00:16:16,008 --> 00:16:18,044
So what do we have to do?

222
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:21,914
Don't worry. I assigned all the roles.

223
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:24,116
Then since we'll be welcoming guests,

224
00:16:24,183 --> 00:16:26,886
let's clean up the village first, okay?

225
00:16:26,953 --> 00:16:29,455
What a pain.
Rural Experience Village, my foot.

226
00:16:29,522 --> 00:16:31,624
What's the point of sitting around?

227
00:16:31,691 --> 00:16:34,660
We should earn whatever we can, right?

228
00:16:36,496 --> 00:16:37,630
Goodness.

229
00:16:37,697 --> 00:16:39,565
You guys help with the cleanup too.

230
00:16:39,632 --> 00:16:41,167
No skipping out, got it?

231
00:16:41,234 --> 00:16:43,836
-Okay.
-Let's go get the brooms.

232
00:16:43,903 --> 00:16:45,238
Hurry up, get moving.

233
00:16:45,304 --> 00:16:46,973
Go on, get going.

234
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,876
Why just stand there staring at me?

235
00:16:49,942 --> 00:16:53,045
-Are you really okay?
-Why wouldn't I be? I'm fine.

236
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:56,949
And don't worry about me.
Just take good care of Yu-na.

237
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:59,318
She must feel stifled
in her room all day.

238
00:16:59,385 --> 00:17:02,655
Take her nearby to get some fresh air.

239
00:17:02,722 --> 00:17:05,625
Anyway, I should go make the website.

240
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:09,595
It's really weird.

241
00:17:09,662 --> 00:17:12,732
She's even worrying about Yu-na.

242
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:16,168
Hey, doesn't she seem strange lately?

243
00:17:16,903 --> 00:17:18,237
She's trying so hard.

244
00:17:18,304 --> 00:17:20,439
Right? You see it too, don't you?

245
00:17:20,506 --> 00:17:23,676
She must be torn up inside over that.

246
00:17:23,743 --> 00:17:25,511
Not that.

247
00:17:26,178 --> 00:17:29,815
-Not that? Then what?
-I'm not telling you!

248
00:17:35,488 --> 00:17:37,490
Why is he getting mad again…

249
00:17:38,324 --> 00:17:39,859
Jeez.

250
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:46,632
Song Hwa-ran, you got a letter.

251
00:17:46,699 --> 00:17:48,935
Looks like it's from Yanbian.

252
00:17:49,001 --> 00:17:52,538
-Thank you.
-Sure, watch out for crackdowns.

253
00:17:55,875 --> 00:17:59,278
Wait, even the mailman knows
Hwa-ran is undocumented?

254
00:18:00,546 --> 00:18:04,850
It's obvious.
You told him again, didn't you?

255
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:07,286
Why is a man such a blabbermouth?

256
00:18:07,353 --> 00:18:09,855
You're the biggest blabbermouth!

257
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:12,091
Mom slapped me with a pig's trotter

258
00:18:12,158 --> 00:18:15,528
-because of you, and it still hurts!
-I told you I was sorry.

259
00:18:15,595 --> 00:18:16,996
Save it.

260
00:18:17,063 --> 00:18:20,499
I'll definitely get my revenge soon,
so mark my words.

261
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:22,335
Good grief.

262
00:18:30,209 --> 00:18:32,578
-What's wrong?
-Um…

263
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:37,083
It's from my younger sibling.
They say my mother is very sick.

264
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:41,153
But she has no money,
so she can't go to the hospital.

265
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:44,790
Then why didn't she say anything
when you called her last time?

266
00:18:45,925 --> 00:18:48,427
She said to keep it a secret from me.

267
00:18:49,061 --> 00:18:50,096
Said she's sorry.

268
00:18:50,162 --> 00:18:51,764
I see.

269
00:18:51,831 --> 00:18:53,666
This is serious.

270
00:18:53,733 --> 00:18:56,202
Can't you borrow money from Mr. Mango?

271
00:18:56,268 --> 00:18:57,770
I can't do that.

272
00:18:57,837 --> 00:19:00,272
I'm already such a burden on him.

273
00:19:00,339 --> 00:19:02,575
I can't borrow money from him too.

274
00:19:03,409 --> 00:19:04,677
But still…

275
00:19:13,786 --> 00:19:17,089
Do you even know how to make a website?

276
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:18,624
-Do you?
-I told you I do.

277
00:19:18,691 --> 00:19:21,127
I'm good with computers. I'm smart.

278
00:19:21,794 --> 00:19:24,563
-I'm a med student.
-This makes me nervous…

279
00:19:25,398 --> 00:19:28,367
The Rural Experience Village
needs this site most, right?

280
00:19:28,434 --> 00:19:30,069
I told you not to worry.

281
00:19:30,136 --> 00:19:33,406
Back in the day,
people even called me a computer whiz…

282
00:19:36,208 --> 00:19:38,944
Oh, no! What's this? What's it doing?

283
00:19:39,545 --> 00:19:42,648
It shouldn't be doing this.
Why is it doing this?

284
00:19:42,715 --> 00:19:44,984
Gosh, seriously! Hey, stop that!

285
00:19:45,051 --> 00:19:47,853
I'm a complete idiot for trusting you!

286
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:50,589
How on earth can I use this now?

287
00:19:50,656 --> 00:19:53,159
I'm sorry. I'll fix it, so don't worry.

288
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:56,028
I'll find the cause if I take it apart.

289
00:19:56,095 --> 00:19:58,130
-Where's a screwdriver?
-You're crazy!

290
00:19:58,197 --> 00:20:00,199
-There's none in there!
-Where is it…

291
00:20:00,266 --> 00:20:02,101
-What's with you?
-A screwdriver…

292
00:20:02,168 --> 00:20:04,804
Hey! You're really driving me crazy!

293
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:07,139
-Seriously…
-What's this? Concert tickets?

294
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:08,207
LEE PIANO RECITAL

295
00:20:08,274 --> 00:20:09,475
Lee Hyeon-seok?

296
00:20:10,142 --> 00:20:11,510
Who is he?

297
00:20:12,845 --> 00:20:14,714
It's nothing. Never mind.

298
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:17,083
Could it be this man?

299
00:20:17,149 --> 00:20:18,684
Min-ho's dad?

300
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:22,788
So it is him.

301
00:20:23,756 --> 00:20:25,391
So, are you going?

302
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:27,993
No.

303
00:20:28,861 --> 00:20:32,498
Can we stop talking about this?

304
00:20:33,265 --> 00:20:34,900
All right.

305
00:20:37,536 --> 00:20:39,572
What on earth happened to this?

306
00:20:39,638 --> 00:20:42,074
The computer isn't ruined, is it?

307
00:20:42,141 --> 00:20:43,576
All because of that brat!

308
00:20:43,642 --> 00:20:45,978
Anyway, nothing goes right. Nothing.

309
00:20:46,045 --> 00:20:47,880
All I need is a screwdriver.

310
00:20:47,947 --> 00:20:49,281
Can you fix it with one?

311
00:20:49,348 --> 00:20:50,583
That's all I need.

312
00:20:50,649 --> 00:20:52,885
-I don't see a screwdriver.
-Stop lying.

313
00:20:52,952 --> 00:20:54,687
Fix this right now, you punk!

314
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:56,188
Do you know if we own one?

315
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:57,490
How would I know that?

316
00:20:57,556 --> 00:20:59,191
If you don't know, who does?

317
00:21:05,564 --> 00:21:07,933
We dig all night and paint all day.

318
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,070
Anyway, is five billion won
really buried in this town?

319
00:21:11,137 --> 00:21:12,905
What if we don't find the money

320
00:21:12,972 --> 00:21:16,142
and just paint murals until we leave?

321
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:18,344
Think pocketing five billion was easy?

322
00:21:18,410 --> 00:21:19,879
If it's too hard, go back.

323
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:22,715
If I go back and those guys catch me,

324
00:21:22,782 --> 00:21:24,784
I'm dead, you bitch!

325
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:31,023
Su-yeon! Oh, there you are.

326
00:21:31,090 --> 00:21:33,859
-Su-yeon, here you are.
-Oh, hello, Village Head.

327
00:21:33,926 --> 00:21:36,262
-Is the mural going well?
-Yes, I suppose.

328
00:21:36,328 --> 00:21:37,963
I have something to ask you.

329
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:40,900
You're here through
the Rural Talent Donation Project?

330
00:21:40,966 --> 00:21:42,101
Excuse me?

331
00:21:42,168 --> 00:21:43,369
Talent Donation?

332
00:21:43,435 --> 00:21:46,639
Yes, the Ministry of Agriculture,
Food and Rural Affairs

333
00:21:46,705 --> 00:21:50,075
sent you to paint murals
for the Rural Talent Donation Project?

334
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:52,912
Oh…

335
00:21:53,546 --> 00:21:56,515
Yes, yes! That's right.
Rural Talent Donation Project.

336
00:21:56,582 --> 00:21:58,717
I knew it.

337
00:21:59,351 --> 00:22:00,486
Our village plans

338
00:22:00,553 --> 00:22:03,122
to carry out
a Rural Experience Village project,

339
00:22:03,189 --> 00:22:06,392
and for it, we need signs, murals, and

340
00:22:06,458 --> 00:22:08,894
banners, so I'd like your help.

341
00:22:08,961 --> 00:22:10,529
Pardon?

342
00:22:11,530 --> 00:22:14,834
It's not too hard, so please help.

343
00:22:15,467 --> 00:22:17,102
Yes, I understand.

344
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:18,204
Great, thank you.

345
00:22:18,270 --> 00:22:20,172
Good luck finishing the mural.

346
00:22:22,942 --> 00:22:26,111
Wow, she asks for a hell of a lot.

347
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:29,548
Why did you have to say
we'd paint murals, of all things?

348
00:22:29,615 --> 00:22:31,884
I'm regretting it too, so shut up!

349
00:22:32,985 --> 00:22:34,620
Su-yeon!

350
00:22:36,755 --> 00:22:38,591
Han-cheol, what is it this time?

351
00:22:38,657 --> 00:22:41,493
I brought these for you to try.

352
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:44,063
The leaves are packed tight inside.

353
00:22:44,129 --> 00:22:46,532
They're really, really sweet.

354
00:22:46,599 --> 00:22:47,933
We'll harvest them soon.

355
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,736
I wanted you both to taste them first.

356
00:22:51,537 --> 00:22:53,038
Okay, thank you.

357
00:22:53,105 --> 00:22:55,674
By the way, is your cold any better?

358
00:22:56,342 --> 00:22:59,378
After eating the porridge you made me,

359
00:22:59,445 --> 00:23:01,780
I recovered completely!

360
00:23:06,886 --> 00:23:07,753
Huh?

361
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:09,355
Oh? Hotteok!

362
00:23:09,421 --> 00:23:11,790
-Oh my.
-Hotteok?

363
00:23:11,857 --> 00:23:14,860
-Is this Hotteok?
-Yes, Hotteok's grown a lot, right?

364
00:23:14,927 --> 00:23:17,196
Hey, where did you get this?

365
00:23:17,263 --> 00:23:20,866
You're finally earning your keep!

366
00:23:20,933 --> 00:23:22,468
Go on, go play.

367
00:23:22,534 --> 00:23:24,603
Come home early for dinner later.

368
00:23:27,873 --> 00:23:32,011
Well, keep up the good work.
I'll be on my way now.

369
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:35,414
Okay, thank you for the cabbage.

370
00:23:38,150 --> 00:23:41,387
Buy some meat to boil and eat with it.

371
00:23:42,454 --> 00:23:46,325
Just put it away. Keep it, keep it.

372
00:23:47,893 --> 00:23:49,461
I'll be going now.

373
00:23:52,631 --> 00:23:54,333
Unbelievable.

374
00:23:55,134 --> 00:23:58,404
Why are you so nice to that jerk?

375
00:23:58,470 --> 00:24:01,740
No way, just because he nursed you,

376
00:24:01,807 --> 00:24:03,842
you're actually interested in him?

377
00:24:03,909 --> 00:24:06,245
Uh, interested? As if.

378
00:24:06,312 --> 00:24:08,047
Stop talking nonsense.

379
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:10,916
If not, fine. Why get so snappy?

380
00:24:12,584 --> 00:24:16,522
But where did that dog get the money?

381
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:21,827
Neither owner nor dog is normal.

382
00:24:24,196 --> 00:24:27,299
Oh, right, have you seen my portfolio?

383
00:24:27,366 --> 00:24:29,168
It's missing.

384
00:24:29,969 --> 00:24:31,437
I haven't seen it.

385
00:24:31,503 --> 00:24:33,405
Jeez, where did it go?

386
00:24:33,472 --> 00:24:36,241
I can't find it anywhere. This is bad.

387
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:39,311
It must be in your room. Why look here?

388
00:24:40,279 --> 00:24:43,282
In my room? What if it's not there?

389
00:24:43,349 --> 00:24:46,685
Hold this for now. I'll go find it.

390
00:24:46,752 --> 00:24:48,053
Darn it.

391
00:24:55,227 --> 00:24:57,563
You rascal, stop drinking so much.

392
00:24:57,629 --> 00:24:58,931
I'm fine.

393
00:24:58,998 --> 00:25:01,867
I drank, but this isn't drunk driving.

394
00:25:01,934 --> 00:25:06,672
Why have you been clinging
to the bottle all day lately?

395
00:25:06,739 --> 00:25:08,774
Did something happen?

396
00:25:08,841 --> 00:25:10,175
Nothing happened.

397
00:25:10,242 --> 00:25:12,711
I don't drink for a reason
and stop without one

398
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:14,313
like some cowardly drinker.

399
00:25:14,380 --> 00:25:15,547
Oh, this guy.

400
00:25:15,614 --> 00:25:19,485
I really like how consistent you are.

401
00:25:25,057 --> 00:25:27,259
Hello, sir.

402
00:25:27,326 --> 00:25:29,595
Hello there. Heading to the shop?

403
00:25:29,661 --> 00:25:31,764
Yes.

404
00:25:31,830 --> 00:25:34,466
Um, sir, I'm late, so I'll get going.

405
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:36,335
Um, Mi-young…

406
00:25:37,669 --> 00:25:39,304
Sang-deuk!

407
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:43,709
Good morning, Sang-deuk!

408
00:25:43,776 --> 00:25:45,744
Bong-ryeon, why did you come here?

409
00:25:46,412 --> 00:25:49,782
I just came because I missed you.

410
00:25:49,848 --> 00:25:52,151
Oh, hello, Grandpa!

411
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:55,654
You're here, my dear daughter-in-law?

412
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:59,091
She's no daughter-in-law!
Grandpa, why are you doing this too?

413
00:25:59,158 --> 00:26:00,959
You know you like it!

414
00:26:01,026 --> 00:26:04,530
Come on, let's go.
I bought some delicious blood sausage.

415
00:26:07,032 --> 00:26:09,334
Mi-young, it's not like that!

416
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:12,137
I'm going crazy here! Let go of me!

417
00:26:12,204 --> 00:26:14,039
Playing hard to get again.

418
00:26:14,106 --> 00:26:16,108
You shy little thing.

419
00:26:17,910 --> 00:26:20,045
Go see a doctor, seriously.

420
00:26:20,112 --> 00:26:21,747
I'm not sick.

421
00:26:23,115 --> 00:26:26,018
It's so nice to get out after so long.

422
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:28,187
This town seems really nice.

423
00:26:28,887 --> 00:26:31,757
The scenery is pretty,
and the people are kind.

424
00:26:31,824 --> 00:26:33,459
Right, Min-gi?

425
00:26:34,793 --> 00:26:38,297
Min-gi, Min-gi.

426
00:26:38,363 --> 00:26:39,498
Huh? What?

427
00:26:39,565 --> 00:26:41,133
What are you thinking about?

428
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:44,903
I'm just a bit worried about Yun-hui.

429
00:26:45,504 --> 00:26:48,373
What happened yesterday
must've really shocked her.

430
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:50,342
Her acting cheerful weighs on me.

431
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:53,078
Is that so?

432
00:26:53,145 --> 00:26:56,115
Don't you think Yun-hui
seems a bit strange lately?

433
00:26:56,181 --> 00:26:58,217
It's good that she's cheerful.

434
00:26:59,084 --> 00:27:01,286
But something feels a bit off.

435
00:27:01,353 --> 00:27:03,322
-Min-gi.
-Huh?

436
00:27:03,388 --> 00:27:05,624
Know you only talked about
Yun-hui today?

437
00:27:05,691 --> 00:27:07,326
Uh… did I do that?

438
00:27:07,392 --> 00:27:09,294
I'm sorry.

439
00:27:09,361 --> 00:27:11,396
Should we go over there too?

440
00:27:11,463 --> 00:27:13,332
There's another nice spot there.

441
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:24,576
It's so chewy.

442
00:27:24,643 --> 00:27:27,880
Lungs are the best with blood sausage.

443
00:27:30,449 --> 00:27:33,185
Mother, please try this too.

444
00:27:33,252 --> 00:27:35,621
-Aah.

445
00:27:38,357 --> 00:27:41,960
It tastes even better
coming from my daughter-in-law.

446
00:27:42,628 --> 00:27:44,696
Who's your daughter-in-law?

447
00:27:44,763 --> 00:27:46,098
Shut up, you bastard!

448
00:27:46,165 --> 00:27:48,667
Oh no, I cursed again.

449
00:27:48,734 --> 00:27:50,869
Father, I apologize.

450
00:27:51,637 --> 00:27:53,372
-Go ahead and eat.
-Okay.

451
00:27:55,274 --> 00:27:58,010
Sang-deuk, say ahh.

452
00:27:58,076 --> 00:27:59,711
I'm fine. Eat plenty yourself.

453
00:27:59,778 --> 00:28:02,447
Hey, punk!
Where are you going, you bastard?

454
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,550
I cursed again. I did it again.

455
00:28:04,616 --> 00:28:07,386
Father, Father, I'm so sorry.

456
00:28:11,423 --> 00:28:14,159
-Sang-deuk, where to?
-None of your business.

457
00:28:14,826 --> 00:28:17,396
Sang-deuk, I'm sick of the mind games.

458
00:28:17,462 --> 00:28:19,264
Can't you stop the mind games?

459
00:28:19,331 --> 00:28:20,465
Mind games, my ass.

460
00:28:21,466 --> 00:28:24,069
I'm not interested in you
in the slightest.

461
00:28:24,136 --> 00:28:26,838
Stop daydreaming and just go home.

462
00:28:30,475 --> 00:28:32,144
Oh my, unbelievable.

463
00:28:32,211 --> 00:28:33,845
Why play so hard to get?

464
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:38,483
Mother!

465
00:28:42,621 --> 00:28:44,456
Hwa-ran!

466
00:28:46,525 --> 00:28:48,994
-Where are you going?
-I am on my way to town.

467
00:28:49,061 --> 00:28:50,629
Why are you going to town?

468
00:28:51,230 --> 00:28:53,632
I am going to collect my unpaid wages.

469
00:28:53,699 --> 00:28:56,635
The factory where I worked
still owes me some money.

470
00:28:57,302 --> 00:28:59,438
My mother's hospital bills are urgent.

471
00:28:59,504 --> 00:29:01,873
And I have nowhere else to get money.

472
00:29:01,940 --> 00:29:04,443
So I am going to plead with them.

473
00:29:04,509 --> 00:29:07,679
Well, I will be on my way now.

474
00:29:09,181 --> 00:29:11,016
Let's go together, then.

475
00:29:11,083 --> 00:29:14,553
Places like that only listen
when a man goes with you.

476
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:18,123
-Ki-jun.
-Uh, don't get the wrong idea.

477
00:29:18,190 --> 00:29:21,159
I'm just doing this
to uphold justice in South Korea.

478
00:29:21,226 --> 00:29:23,895
It's not because I like you.

479
00:29:24,730 --> 00:29:26,365
Let's go.

480
00:29:35,007 --> 00:29:36,174
Is this the place?

481
00:29:38,343 --> 00:29:40,212
Hwa-ran, wait here for now.

482
00:29:40,279 --> 00:29:41,813
I'll go talk to them first.

483
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:44,116
Um, will you be all right on your own?

484
00:29:45,083 --> 00:29:48,287
Hwa-ran, are you worried about me?

485
00:29:50,289 --> 00:29:52,491
My nickname back in school was

486
00:29:52,557 --> 00:29:54,993
Inspiring Generation,
Inspiring Generation.

487
00:29:55,060 --> 00:29:58,096
I fought so well, my opponents
were moved and inspired.

488
00:29:58,163 --> 00:30:00,699
That's how I got this nickname.

489
00:30:00,766 --> 00:30:02,868
Hwa-ran, play in the snow and wait.

490
00:30:02,934 --> 00:30:04,069
I'll get it quickly.

491
00:30:18,116 --> 00:30:20,285
Who is in charge here?

492
00:30:20,352 --> 00:30:21,520
Who are you?

493
00:30:21,586 --> 00:30:24,556
Get the person in charge out here.
Don't ask who I am.

494
00:30:25,290 --> 00:30:28,193
Everyone went out to eat,
so what brings you here…

495
00:30:28,260 --> 00:30:31,797
It's none of your business.
I'll use the chair until they're back.

496
00:30:31,863 --> 00:30:33,632
Get me some coffee, strong.

497
00:30:33,699 --> 00:30:35,801
-Excuse me.
-Don't talk to me!

498
00:30:51,817 --> 00:30:53,352
Did you look for it?

499
00:30:53,418 --> 00:30:55,620
No matter how hard I look, it's gone.

500
00:30:55,687 --> 00:30:57,789
It's so precious to me.

501
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:59,358
This is driving me crazy.

502
00:30:59,424 --> 00:31:02,694
If it's that precious,
you should've put it away.

503
00:31:09,167 --> 00:31:11,570
Huh? What's that?

504
00:31:12,337 --> 00:31:15,040
This dog brought money again.

505
00:31:15,107 --> 00:31:17,843
Where does it keep getting this money?

506
00:31:17,909 --> 00:31:19,244
Wait!

507
00:31:19,311 --> 00:31:21,446
Look at the dirt on its paws and mouth.

508
00:31:21,513 --> 00:31:23,448
Think it dug this out of the ground?

509
00:31:23,515 --> 00:31:25,183
The ground?

510
00:31:25,884 --> 00:31:27,285
Hold on.

511
00:31:27,352 --> 00:31:29,321
You don't think…

512
00:31:29,388 --> 00:31:32,691
it dug this up from where
the five billion won is buried?

513
00:31:32,758 --> 00:31:34,426
Come on, no way.

514
00:31:34,493 --> 00:31:36,495
It's totally possible!

515
00:31:37,129 --> 00:31:38,597
You think so?

516
00:31:38,663 --> 00:31:40,866
-Oh!
-Su-yeon!

517
00:31:40,932 --> 00:31:42,567
-Huh?
-Hotteok, Hotteok!

518
00:31:42,634 --> 00:31:44,035
Hi, Han-cheol.

519
00:31:44,736 --> 00:31:45,771
Hotteok bother you?

520
00:31:45,837 --> 00:31:48,673
I told you not to bother Su-yeon
while she's working!

521
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:51,376
-Come on, let's go.
-Um, Han-cheol.

522
00:31:51,443 --> 00:31:52,611
Yes? What is it?

523
00:31:52,677 --> 00:31:55,580
Could you help me paint the mural?

524
00:31:55,647 --> 00:31:58,150
I have so much work for the town event.

525
00:31:58,216 --> 00:32:00,018
I'm not very good at painting…

526
00:32:00,085 --> 00:32:04,456
Painting is no big deal.
Just swipe a few lines with the brush.

527
00:32:04,523 --> 00:32:06,191
Um…

528
00:32:07,359 --> 00:32:10,195
Please, I'm begging you.

529
00:32:10,962 --> 00:32:12,597
Pretty please?

530
00:32:20,772 --> 00:32:24,609
When you ask with a look like that,
I really can't say no.

531
00:32:25,177 --> 00:32:27,145
I'm melting, just melting.

532
00:32:28,380 --> 00:32:30,182
I'll help you out.

533
00:32:30,248 --> 00:32:32,851
Sorry, is it okay if we take a break?

534
00:32:32,918 --> 00:32:35,854
Of course, take a good, long rest.

535
00:32:35,921 --> 00:32:37,923
I'll paint it all myself, all of it.

536
00:32:37,989 --> 00:32:39,558
Thank you.

537
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:42,427
By the way, couldn't we take Hotteok…

538
00:32:42,494 --> 00:32:44,863
with us for a little while?

539
00:32:45,464 --> 00:32:48,500
This dog is just so cute!

540
00:32:49,401 --> 00:32:53,505
You've completely fallen
for Hotteok's charm again.

541
00:32:55,607 --> 00:32:59,644
Still, don't fall too hard for Hotteok.

542
00:33:00,378 --> 00:33:02,247
It makes me jealous.

543
00:33:04,149 --> 00:33:07,085
-We'll be back soon.
-Yes, see you soon, see you soon.

544
00:33:07,752 --> 00:33:08,954
Yes, see you soon.

545
00:33:09,020 --> 00:33:10,989
Go on, Hotteok! Have fun!

546
00:33:19,264 --> 00:33:21,066
Yes, hello. Yes, yes.

547
00:33:21,733 --> 00:33:24,135
Yes, it's ready already?

548
00:33:24,202 --> 00:33:27,305
Yes, thank you. Please ship it to me.

549
00:33:28,907 --> 00:33:31,810
Excuse me, may I ask what the issue is…

550
00:33:31,877 --> 00:33:36,047
The person in charge!
I said I'll talk when they get here.

551
00:33:42,420 --> 00:33:44,623
What's going on?

552
00:33:49,728 --> 00:33:51,196
Manager.

553
00:33:52,898 --> 00:33:55,634
He kept asking to see who's in charge.

554
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:58,069
Hey, what's this about?

555
00:33:58,136 --> 00:34:00,906
Um, well, the thing is…

556
00:34:00,972 --> 00:34:04,342
I came for the unpaid wages
of Song Hwa-ran, who worked here.

557
00:34:04,409 --> 00:34:07,579
Here we go again. Not this again.

558
00:34:07,646 --> 00:34:10,782
Hey, I told you we'd pay later.

559
00:34:10,849 --> 00:34:14,686
Later? It's an urgent matter.
Give it to me now, right now!

560
00:34:14,753 --> 00:34:16,688
I won't move an inch until you pay.

561
00:34:16,755 --> 00:34:18,790
This guy, seriously…

562
00:34:18,857 --> 00:34:21,793
Get out before things get ugly, buddy!

563
00:34:21,860 --> 00:34:23,361
I can't go!

564
00:34:23,428 --> 00:34:24,996
I won't leave until you pay.

565
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:26,731
And that's final.

566
00:34:29,935 --> 00:34:32,037
Why is it so loud in here?

567
00:34:38,076 --> 00:34:41,079
This guy's causing a ruckus
over Song Hwa-ran's wages.

568
00:34:41,146 --> 00:34:42,914
What's your problem?

569
00:34:47,118 --> 00:34:49,754
How dare you pull that in here!

570
00:34:53,658 --> 00:34:55,627
Please… give me the money.

571
00:34:55,694 --> 00:34:58,797
We… really need it
for Hwa-ran's mom's hospital bills.

572
00:35:04,235 --> 00:35:06,338
That's not our problem.

573
00:35:07,539 --> 00:35:10,075
What'll you do if the boss shows up?

574
00:35:10,141 --> 00:35:11,710
Huh?

575
00:35:12,510 --> 00:35:16,381
Boss or chairman, I'm not scared,
so just give me the money! Huh?

576
00:35:17,282 --> 00:35:18,683
What is this?

577
00:35:18,750 --> 00:35:21,620
Why is the office so noisy?

578
00:35:22,387 --> 00:35:24,089
-Boss.
-Hello.

579
00:35:24,155 --> 00:35:26,024
Who are you?

580
00:35:26,091 --> 00:35:28,093
Why are you making a scene here?

581
00:35:28,927 --> 00:35:30,595
Well, that's… Um…

582
00:35:30,662 --> 00:35:33,398
I can't remember why I came here…

583
00:35:33,465 --> 00:35:34,833
I remember now, sir.

584
00:35:34,899 --> 00:35:36,167
Um…

585
00:35:36,234 --> 00:35:39,804
if you could… kindly pay
Song Hwa-ran's unpaid wages,

586
00:35:40,472 --> 00:35:42,941
I would consider it…
an honor to my family.

587
00:35:45,110 --> 00:35:46,444
What did you say?

588
00:35:46,511 --> 00:35:49,147
Oh, you're angry. Then, um…

589
00:35:49,214 --> 00:35:50,582
even… just half…

590
00:35:50,649 --> 00:35:52,717
Argh!

591
00:36:00,959 --> 00:36:02,594
Ki-jun!

592
00:36:02,661 --> 00:36:04,062
Ow, ouch!

593
00:36:04,129 --> 00:36:05,830
What kind of company is this?

594
00:36:05,897 --> 00:36:07,298
Do they promote by size?

595
00:36:07,365 --> 00:36:09,834
Then how big is the chairman?

596
00:36:10,902 --> 00:36:13,405
-Nothing wrong?
-I think something's wrong, ow.

597
00:36:13,471 --> 00:36:15,407
Forget it. Just give up.

598
00:36:16,608 --> 00:36:19,144
No, I can't give up.

599
00:36:19,210 --> 00:36:20,712
They picked the wrong guy.

600
00:36:20,779 --> 00:36:22,447
I will get that money today.

601
00:36:22,514 --> 00:36:24,215
Just count on it and wait.

602
00:36:27,919 --> 00:36:29,387
In the summer, that place…

603
00:36:29,454 --> 00:36:33,558
used to have tons of fish,
so we'd catch them all the time.

604
00:36:40,632 --> 00:36:42,033
Oh?

605
00:36:42,100 --> 00:36:44,636
What's this? Were you two on a date?

606
00:36:44,703 --> 00:36:48,373
-We just went for a walk.
-You did?

607
00:36:49,674 --> 00:36:51,843
Next time, ask me before you go.

608
00:36:51,910 --> 00:36:53,945
I'll tell you a fantastic spot.

609
00:36:58,450 --> 00:37:01,152
Gosh, I should go feed the cows.

610
00:37:02,153 --> 00:37:04,456
Hye-gyo and Tae-hui
must be hungry, right?

611
00:37:04,522 --> 00:37:06,357
Can't let them go hungry.

612
00:37:11,396 --> 00:37:13,064
Min-gi.

613
00:37:15,433 --> 00:37:17,402
Go on inside first.

614
00:37:39,457 --> 00:37:41,259
Yun-hui.

615
00:37:42,327 --> 00:37:44,996
Oh? What is it?

616
00:37:45,063 --> 00:37:48,133
Was the date fun? Did you like it?

617
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:53,338
Why didn't you at least
give Yu-na a kiss after so long?

618
00:37:54,372 --> 00:37:55,940
Stop it.

619
00:37:56,007 --> 00:37:58,910
-What?
-Stop forcing a smile.

620
00:37:58,977 --> 00:38:02,046
-I hate seeing it.
-What's that supposed to mean?

621
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:04,182
Why on earth are you like this lately?

622
00:38:04,249 --> 00:38:07,919
-What about me?
-You seem like someone else, somehow.

623
00:38:07,986 --> 00:38:08,853
Just different.

624
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:11,823
Come on, how am I different?

625
00:38:13,091 --> 00:38:15,794
And whether I changed or not,
what's it to you?

626
00:38:15,860 --> 00:38:17,362
Because I care about you.

627
00:38:17,428 --> 00:38:19,130
I told you, didn't I?

628
00:38:19,197 --> 00:38:21,566
From now on,
stop caring about Min-ho and me.

629
00:38:21,633 --> 00:38:23,902
How can I stop caring when I do?

630
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:26,137
Why do you care about me? Why?

631
00:38:26,204 --> 00:38:27,372
I don't know either!

632
00:38:27,438 --> 00:38:30,809
Why I care about your every
expression, look, and tone,

633
00:38:30,875 --> 00:38:32,510
I have no idea either.

634
00:38:33,178 --> 00:38:35,346
You make me feel miserable to the end.

635
00:38:35,413 --> 00:38:36,714
What? What did I do?

636
00:38:36,781 --> 00:38:39,450
The reason you care about me,

637
00:38:39,517 --> 00:38:41,753
a single mom and the Village Head,

638
00:38:41,820 --> 00:38:45,123
is just pity and sympathy
for your old first love.

639
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:46,758
Am I wrong?

640
00:38:47,325 --> 00:38:50,028
-What?
-But I really don't want

641
00:38:50,094 --> 00:38:53,097
that kind of pity at all.

642
00:38:53,164 --> 00:38:54,833
So I'll say it one more time,

643
00:38:54,899 --> 00:38:59,637
stop caring about my tone,
my look, and my expressions.

644
00:38:59,704 --> 00:39:01,973
Because it really offends me.

645
00:39:05,710 --> 00:39:07,545
Fine! I get it.

646
00:39:07,612 --> 00:39:11,382
From now on,
I won't care about you even this much.

647
00:39:11,449 --> 00:39:13,918
So don't you worry, got it?

648
00:39:13,985 --> 00:39:15,687
Darn it.

649
00:39:44,716 --> 00:39:46,885
You guys messed with the wrong person.

650
00:39:46,951 --> 00:39:48,553
Think I'd leave empty-handed?

651
00:39:48,620 --> 00:39:52,824
If I don't get paid, I'm taking
all your stuff instead, you bastards!

652
00:40:07,839 --> 00:40:10,575
Excuse me, Ki-jun!

653
00:40:10,642 --> 00:40:12,076
Ki-jun!

654
00:40:12,143 --> 00:40:13,778
Are… you all right?

655
00:40:24,656 --> 00:40:27,091
Gosh, this is such a pain in the neck!

656
00:40:27,158 --> 00:40:28,793
Rural Experience Village? Ha!

657
00:40:28,860 --> 00:40:33,298
That woman Yun-hui is a real pro
at starting new things, a total pro.

658
00:40:34,032 --> 00:40:35,500
Big brother!

659
00:40:38,836 --> 00:40:40,705
Have some of this first.

660
00:40:41,539 --> 00:40:43,441
-What's that now?
-This?

661
00:40:43,508 --> 00:40:46,544
I poured my heart into
developing this bokbunjaccino.

662
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:48,680
Bokbunja… A bokbunjaccino!

663
00:40:48,746 --> 00:40:52,617
Yes, it's healthy and tastes great.
How about it? Sounds tasty, right?

664
00:40:52,684 --> 00:40:53,885
Sure, sure, sure.

665
00:40:53,952 --> 00:40:55,019
Guzzle it yourself!

666
00:40:55,086 --> 00:40:56,988
Didn't I say to stop this nonsense?

667
00:40:57,055 --> 00:41:00,091
You think this will make me
open a coffee shop for you?

668
00:41:00,158 --> 00:41:01,859
Not in a million years!

669
00:41:01,926 --> 00:41:03,628
Big brother, open one for me.

670
00:41:03,695 --> 00:41:06,164
I can't work part-time jobs forever.

671
00:41:06,230 --> 00:41:09,901
I'll work so hard this time,
so open me a coffee shop, big brother.

672
00:41:09,968 --> 00:41:12,704
Give me a break.
How many times have you done this?

673
00:41:12,770 --> 00:41:15,039
You know how much money you've blown?

674
00:41:15,106 --> 00:41:18,576
I told you, this time is different.
I swear I can do a great job!

675
00:41:18,643 --> 00:41:20,311
I said forget it!

676
00:41:20,378 --> 00:41:23,982
Talk all day long if you want.
I won't even bat an eye.

677
00:41:26,217 --> 00:41:29,687
Are you really going to be like this?
You're going to regret it.

678
00:41:29,754 --> 00:41:31,823
Regret it? Oh, I'm so scared.

679
00:41:31,889 --> 00:41:35,059
What are you going to do?
What'll you do, you little brat?

680
00:41:39,897 --> 00:41:41,332
What are you doing now?

681
00:41:42,633 --> 00:41:46,871
I'll eat every last strawberry here
until you open a coffee shop for me!

682
00:41:48,106 --> 00:41:50,808
You're pulling every dirty trick…

683
00:41:55,046 --> 00:41:56,614
Is she a sister or a nemesis?

684
00:41:56,681 --> 00:41:58,016
She's driving me crazy.

685
00:41:58,082 --> 00:42:00,051
Who on earth does she take after--

686
00:42:00,118 --> 00:42:01,786
What's wrong with you again?

687
00:42:01,853 --> 00:42:03,688
That darn girl wants a café.

688
00:42:03,755 --> 00:42:05,623
She's staging a protest! A protest!

689
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:07,525
Gosh, what an immature brat.

690
00:42:07,592 --> 00:42:09,193
Is the strawberry jam ready?

691
00:42:09,260 --> 00:42:12,997
I don't know.
My arm's killing me. Can't I stop now?

692
00:42:13,064 --> 00:42:14,966
What do you mean? Not even close.

693
00:42:15,033 --> 00:42:17,301
Since we'll sell it to tour guests,

694
00:42:17,368 --> 00:42:18,970
stir well so it won't burn.

695
00:42:19,037 --> 00:42:21,205
I'll go order the boxes and be back.

696
00:42:21,272 --> 00:42:24,208
-Put it in storage when it's done.
-All right.

697
00:42:24,275 --> 00:42:27,011
Gosh, making people work is so hard.

698
00:42:27,078 --> 00:42:29,981
I'm seriously exhausted to death.

699
00:42:32,884 --> 00:42:35,253
My, what are you doing here, Mrs. Kim?

700
00:42:35,319 --> 00:42:37,188
Oh my, Mr. Han!

701
00:42:37,255 --> 00:42:39,891
Oh, you're making strawberry jam.

702
00:42:39,957 --> 00:42:42,994
-May I give you a hand?
-No, that's all right.

703
00:42:43,061 --> 00:42:46,364
Not at all.
It must be hard on such slender arms.

704
00:42:46,431 --> 00:42:49,734
-Let me help you with that.
-Oh, I'm fine, really…

705
00:43:09,921 --> 00:43:11,255
Should I put it here?

706
00:43:11,322 --> 00:43:12,990
Yes. Phew.

707
00:43:13,925 --> 00:43:16,861
We finished quickly thanks to you.
Thank you.

708
00:43:16,928 --> 00:43:19,564
Not at all. If you ever need a hand,

709
00:43:19,630 --> 00:43:21,466
please let me know anytime.

710
00:43:21,532 --> 00:43:22,900
Yes, I will.

711
00:43:22,967 --> 00:43:26,737
Oh, but it's really freezing in here.

712
00:43:26,804 --> 00:43:28,906
It is a refrigerator, after all.

713
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:31,876
Let's hurry out before we catch a cold.

714
00:43:31,943 --> 00:43:33,744
No, you go first, Mr. Han.

715
00:43:33,811 --> 00:43:38,116
"Ladies first," they say. After you.

716
00:43:44,222 --> 00:43:46,190
Huh? Why isn't this working?

717
00:43:46,257 --> 00:43:50,261
Goodness, Mr. Han, please try it.
Why won't it open?

718
00:43:55,900 --> 00:43:57,735
This should open from inside too.

719
00:43:57,802 --> 00:44:00,204
It opened fine before. It won't open?

720
00:44:00,271 --> 00:44:02,540
-We're in trouble.
-Is it broken?

721
00:44:02,607 --> 00:44:03,908
What?

722
00:44:03,975 --> 00:44:06,043
Hello? Over here!

723
00:44:06,110 --> 00:44:08,346
There are people in here!

724
00:44:10,448 --> 00:44:11,782
Over here!

725
00:44:12,683 --> 00:44:15,319
Oh no, my phone has no signal either.

726
00:44:15,386 --> 00:44:18,422
-What?
-My phone has no signal either.

727
00:44:18,489 --> 00:44:20,791
We're in real trouble, aren't we?

728
00:44:23,728 --> 00:44:27,098
Just how far is that dog going?

729
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:29,634
Does it know where the money's buried?

730
00:44:30,301 --> 00:44:32,436
It brought cash back twice, not once!

731
00:44:32,503 --> 00:44:35,373
Nothing to lose, so let's follow it.

732
00:44:41,579 --> 00:44:43,514
Oh, it looks like it's digging!

733
00:44:43,581 --> 00:44:45,383
-Let's go, let's go!
-Okay!

734
00:44:47,818 --> 00:44:50,922
This little rascal is pretty clever.

735
00:44:50,988 --> 00:44:53,357
So we just dig right here?

736
00:44:53,424 --> 00:44:56,027
Okay, let's dig.

737
00:45:02,567 --> 00:45:04,468
What is this?

738
00:45:13,177 --> 00:45:15,780
It's a bra, a brassiere.

739
00:45:17,281 --> 00:45:20,551
And an enviable C-cup at that.

740
00:45:21,619 --> 00:45:24,088
She's even busty, the nerve of her.

741
00:45:24,155 --> 00:45:27,391
I've never seen such a perverted dog.

742
00:45:30,595 --> 00:45:32,230
Oh? There it goes again!

743
00:45:32,296 --> 00:45:33,931
Come on, hurry up!

744
00:45:35,299 --> 00:45:37,535
Look, it's digging! That must be it.

745
00:45:37,602 --> 00:45:39,904
-Let's go, let's go!
-Let's go see.

746
00:45:41,272 --> 00:45:42,740
Here, this must be it.

747
00:45:42,807 --> 00:45:44,141
Let's dig.

748
00:45:52,149 --> 00:45:54,285
Oh! Wait, this…

749
00:45:54,352 --> 00:45:57,288
feels like paper.

750
00:45:57,955 --> 00:46:00,591
Even the color is bluish-green.

751
00:46:09,066 --> 00:46:10,668
Darn it.

752
00:46:10,735 --> 00:46:14,338
What kind of dog
is into such dirty stuff?

753
00:46:14,405 --> 00:46:18,643
Like his owner, he's a total pervert.

754
00:46:19,710 --> 00:46:21,712
I'm seriously losing my mind.

755
00:46:25,082 --> 00:46:26,117
He's off again.

756
00:46:26,183 --> 00:46:28,319
Hey, just stop already.

757
00:46:28,386 --> 00:46:30,821
I'm afraid to see what comes up next.

758
00:46:30,888 --> 00:46:32,957
Let's go just one last time.

759
00:46:33,024 --> 00:46:35,092
If it's nothing again, we'll give up.

760
00:46:38,696 --> 00:46:40,398
Hey, wait!

761
00:46:40,464 --> 00:46:42,767
Where is he running off to so fast?

762
00:46:43,434 --> 00:46:44,602
What?

763
00:46:44,669 --> 00:46:48,606
But isn't this where
we painted the mural?

764
00:46:48,673 --> 00:46:51,776
They say you overlook
what's right under your nose.

765
00:46:51,842 --> 00:46:54,278
Could it have been buried right here?

766
00:46:54,345 --> 00:46:56,013
What?

767
00:47:00,251 --> 00:47:03,321
But what's he doing with my clothes?

768
00:47:04,288 --> 00:47:05,956
I'm not sure.

769
00:47:11,062 --> 00:47:13,631
My… My money?

770
00:47:14,465 --> 00:47:16,300
Darn it.

771
00:47:16,367 --> 00:47:20,304
No wonder 10,000 won kept disappearing.

772
00:47:20,371 --> 00:47:23,274
This bastard of a dog stole it.

773
00:47:24,842 --> 00:47:26,043
Hey, you punk.

774
00:47:26,110 --> 00:47:30,214
You're just a dog,
and you steal people's money?

775
00:47:30,281 --> 00:47:32,883
You're a pervert, and now a thief too?

776
00:47:32,950 --> 00:47:36,454
You're a dog that's worse than a dog!

777
00:47:36,520 --> 00:47:38,089
Why is it so loud?

778
00:47:38,155 --> 00:47:40,224
You're not even a single mouthful.

779
00:47:40,291 --> 00:47:41,892
How dare you live like that?

780
00:47:41,959 --> 00:47:45,463
Excuse me, why are you
getting mad at someone else's dog?

781
00:47:45,529 --> 00:47:47,898
Your dog stole my money.

782
00:47:47,965 --> 00:47:50,000
How on earth did you train him?

783
00:47:50,067 --> 00:47:51,936
What are you talking about?

784
00:47:52,002 --> 00:47:54,739
My Hotteok is not that kind of dog.

785
00:47:54,805 --> 00:47:59,043
I saw him steal money from my clothes,
and you're still playing innocent?

786
00:48:01,212 --> 00:48:03,547
Uh… Is that really true?

787
00:48:09,019 --> 00:48:11,789
Hotteok, did you really steal it?

788
00:48:12,456 --> 00:48:14,158
Did you?

789
00:48:14,225 --> 00:48:17,762
Look your big brother in the eye
and say something, you brat!

790
00:48:17,828 --> 00:48:19,430
Please, that's enough.

791
00:48:19,497 --> 00:48:21,732
How would a dog know any better?

792
00:48:25,136 --> 00:48:27,571
Su-yeon, I am truly sorry.

793
00:48:27,638 --> 00:48:31,142
It is entirely my fault
for not training Hotteok properly.

794
00:48:31,208 --> 00:48:35,112
I apologize on Hotteok's behalf.

795
00:48:35,179 --> 00:48:37,948
No, not at all. It's okay.

796
00:48:38,616 --> 00:48:40,050
Hotteok.

797
00:48:40,785 --> 00:48:42,453
You, follow me.

798
00:48:42,520 --> 00:48:44,422
I'm really disappointed in you.

799
00:48:44,488 --> 00:48:46,791
Is that how I trained you?

800
00:48:47,825 --> 00:48:50,895
Follow me, follow me!

801
00:48:53,264 --> 00:48:56,834
The owner and his dog aren't normal.
They're just not normal.

802
00:48:58,335 --> 00:49:01,505
Where on earth is that five billion?

803
00:49:02,773 --> 00:49:04,442
Oh, my gosh!

804
00:49:05,810 --> 00:49:08,078
What's this now?

805
00:49:12,316 --> 00:49:15,219
-Gently, gently.
-I'm sorry.

806
00:49:15,886 --> 00:49:17,288
Gently, gently.

807
00:49:20,858 --> 00:49:23,594
I told you to drop it.
Why keep being so stubborn?

808
00:49:23,661 --> 00:49:25,062
They're so shameless.

809
00:49:25,129 --> 00:49:28,098
How could they cheat you
out of your hard-earned money?

810
00:49:28,766 --> 00:49:31,068
-Those jerks, I'll--
-Forget it.

811
00:49:31,135 --> 00:49:35,473
Just stop now.
You'll only get hurt more for nothing.

812
00:49:35,539 --> 00:49:38,442
What are you talking about?
I got something out of it.

813
00:49:38,976 --> 00:49:40,110
What do you mean?

814
00:49:40,177 --> 00:49:42,780
You really think I left empty-handed?

815
00:49:45,216 --> 00:49:47,184
Ta-da!

816
00:49:47,251 --> 00:49:49,954
Isn't this soap?

817
00:49:50,020 --> 00:49:52,857
It's not that I can't fight.
I just let them hit me.

818
00:49:52,923 --> 00:49:56,627
When they were off guard hitting me,
I swiped this soap. Swipe, swipe!

819
00:49:58,395 --> 00:49:59,497
Here, take these.

820
00:49:59,563 --> 00:50:01,565
Once I heal up and make a new plan,

821
00:50:01,632 --> 00:50:02,600
I'll get you more.

822
00:50:02,666 --> 00:50:05,035
We should at least take these
instead of pay.

823
00:50:05,102 --> 00:50:07,371
-Ki-jun.
-Don't get the wrong idea.

824
00:50:07,438 --> 00:50:09,573
I'm upholding justice in South Korea.

825
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,308
It's not because I like you.

826
00:50:11,375 --> 00:50:13,644
Yes, I got it.

827
00:50:13,711 --> 00:50:14,945
There's more.

828
00:50:15,679 --> 00:50:17,248
Let's get going.

829
00:50:17,314 --> 00:50:19,283
Hwa-ran.

830
00:50:19,350 --> 00:50:23,187
Could you help hold me up?

831
00:50:23,754 --> 00:50:25,456
I don't think I can walk.

832
00:50:26,056 --> 00:50:28,425
I can't take a step. It hurts so much.

833
00:50:30,628 --> 00:50:32,263
I think I sprained my ankle.

834
00:50:32,329 --> 00:50:35,032
-Are you okay?
-I don't think I'm okay.

835
00:50:35,099 --> 00:50:36,734
Oh, gosh.

836
00:50:37,935 --> 00:50:39,770
I've never been here before.

837
00:50:40,304 --> 00:50:42,606
Didn't we catch a pheasant
on that mountain?

838
00:50:43,440 --> 00:50:45,242
Over here!

839
00:50:45,309 --> 00:50:47,211
Is anyone out there? Anyone?

840
00:50:47,278 --> 00:50:49,113
Someone's in here!

841
00:50:50,381 --> 00:50:51,582
Over here!

842
00:50:52,383 --> 00:50:54,151
It's no use.

843
00:50:54,218 --> 00:50:56,287
We're too far from the village.

844
00:50:57,121 --> 00:50:58,556
No one will hear us.

845
00:50:58,622 --> 00:51:00,424
-Mrs. Kim.
-Yes.

846
00:51:00,491 --> 00:51:02,059
Are you cold?

847
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:04,562
This is really bad.

848
00:51:04,628 --> 00:51:06,397
This just won't do.

849
00:51:16,774 --> 00:51:19,176
You feel much better now, don't you?

850
00:51:19,243 --> 00:51:23,981
Yes, I do, but Mr. Han,
what will you do in this cold?

851
00:51:24,582 --> 00:51:26,216
Well, I…

852
00:51:27,918 --> 00:51:31,555
do not get cold if I move like this.

853
00:51:42,967 --> 00:51:45,603
Oh my, that wild masculinity.

854
00:51:53,010 --> 00:51:56,180
I'm here now. You can head on back.

855
00:51:57,181 --> 00:51:59,883
And thank you for today.

856
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:03,153
Could you stop saying thank you?

857
00:52:03,220 --> 00:52:06,056
-I'm sorry.
-And stop saying you're sorry, too.

858
00:52:06,123 --> 00:52:09,760
Okay, got it. You go on ahead, then.

859
00:52:09,827 --> 00:52:12,596
I'll stay and clean that up first.

860
00:52:12,663 --> 00:52:14,932
Since I'm here, let's do it together.

861
00:52:14,999 --> 00:52:16,700
What do I need to do?

862
00:52:28,278 --> 00:52:31,582
Mr. Han, are you all right?

863
00:52:32,683 --> 00:52:35,819
Mr. Han, Mr. Han.

864
00:52:35,886 --> 00:52:37,988
Mr. Han!

865
00:52:40,257 --> 00:52:42,493
Wait, his body is ice-cold.

866
00:52:42,559 --> 00:52:46,363
Oh, no, what do I do?
He's going to die like this!

867
00:52:46,430 --> 00:52:48,499
Mr. Han.

868
00:52:50,034 --> 00:52:53,170
Mr. Han, please wake up.

869
00:52:53,237 --> 00:52:56,140
Mr. Han, you can't die like this.

870
00:52:56,206 --> 00:52:59,109
Mr. Han, don't leave me behind.

871
00:52:59,176 --> 00:53:00,511
Mr. Han!

872
00:53:28,072 --> 00:53:30,207
Mrs. Kim.

873
00:53:31,775 --> 00:53:34,244
Mr. Han, are you awake?

874
00:53:34,311 --> 00:53:37,448
Mrs. Kim, your warm tears

875
00:53:37,514 --> 00:53:40,117
seem to have awakened me.

876
00:53:40,184 --> 00:53:42,019
Thank you.

877
00:53:42,720 --> 00:53:44,388
Not at all.

878
00:53:54,131 --> 00:53:57,534
What are you two doing in here?

879
00:53:57,601 --> 00:53:59,837
Hwa-ran, well, the thing is…

880
00:53:59,903 --> 00:54:02,639
it was just an accident.
The freezer door broke.

881
00:54:02,706 --> 00:54:06,744
Go on, keep doing what you were doing.

882
00:54:06,810 --> 00:54:09,179
I didn't see a thing.

883
00:54:10,314 --> 00:54:13,951
Hey, where are you going?
It's a misunderstanding!

884
00:54:23,060 --> 00:54:24,394
I'm losing my mind.

885
00:54:24,461 --> 00:54:27,564
The door just had to break right then.

886
00:54:27,631 --> 00:54:28,966
Hello, ma'am!

887
00:54:29,032 --> 00:54:31,869
I heard you're dating Mr. Han?
Wow, must be nice!

888
00:54:31,935 --> 00:54:33,537
-What?
-In the shed, I heard

889
00:54:33,604 --> 00:54:35,372
you rolled around and did it all.

890
00:54:35,439 --> 00:54:36,940
-Did it all?
-Did it all.

891
00:54:37,007 --> 00:54:39,643
-Who said that?
-Ki-jun said he saw it all.

892
00:54:39,710 --> 00:54:41,044
Goodbye, then!

893
00:54:41,111 --> 00:54:43,614
Ma'am, ma'am!
I heard you're marrying Mr. Han?

894
00:54:43,680 --> 00:54:44,748
-What?
-And I heard

895
00:54:44,815 --> 00:54:46,550
you're pregnant at your age too?

896
00:54:46,617 --> 00:54:48,118
-Really?
-Congratulations!

897
00:54:48,185 --> 00:54:49,319
A baby at her age!

898
00:54:49,386 --> 00:54:51,588
No, that's not true, Yun-hui!

899
00:54:51,655 --> 00:54:53,357
Ma'am!

900
00:54:53,423 --> 00:54:55,626
Is it true you'll be my stepmother?

901
00:54:55,692 --> 00:54:57,027
It's not true, right?

902
00:54:57,094 --> 00:54:59,463
-What? Your stepmom?
-Mom!

903
00:55:00,130 --> 00:55:02,900
I can't face the neighbors!
What is going on here?

904
00:55:02,966 --> 00:55:05,869
Getting a sibling at my age?
Does that make any sense?

905
00:55:05,936 --> 00:55:08,939
Since when have you been seeing In-ki?

906
00:55:09,006 --> 00:55:11,642
This old guy is my older brother now?

907
00:55:11,708 --> 00:55:13,310
No way!

908
00:55:13,377 --> 00:55:16,547
No, that's not it. I mean, how…

909
00:55:16,613 --> 00:55:19,249
How is it not?
The rumor's already all over town!

910
00:55:19,316 --> 00:55:21,351
I'm too ashamed to face the town.

911
00:55:21,418 --> 00:55:23,420
Man-gu!

912
00:55:24,087 --> 00:55:27,491
That little punk Ki-jun, I swear!

913
00:55:31,795 --> 00:55:34,031
I must clear up the misunderstanding.

914
00:55:34,097 --> 00:55:36,834
But what's taking Mi-young so long?

915
00:55:37,467 --> 00:55:40,237
Drinking that rice wine
makes me have to pee again.

916
00:55:44,508 --> 00:55:46,944
What if she shows up
while I'm peeing again?

917
00:56:01,758 --> 00:56:04,828
-What are you doing?
-No, no!

918
00:56:04,895 --> 00:56:07,998
I wasn't peeing! Definitely not!

919
00:56:08,065 --> 00:56:10,901
-But what brings you here?
-Huh?

920
00:56:10,968 --> 00:56:14,504
Mi-young, what you saw earlier
was a misunderstanding.

921
00:56:14,571 --> 00:56:16,473
There's nothing between her and me.

922
00:56:16,540 --> 00:56:18,742
Why are you telling me that?

923
00:56:18,809 --> 00:56:20,777
I don't care who you date.

924
00:56:20,844 --> 00:56:22,846
Mi-young, why are you being like this?

925
00:56:23,614 --> 00:56:26,383
I'm tired, so I'm going inside.

926
00:56:27,150 --> 00:56:28,452
Mi-young.

927
00:56:28,518 --> 00:56:31,488
When someone is talking to you,

928
00:56:31,555 --> 00:56:33,523
you should hear them out to the end.

929
00:56:34,224 --> 00:56:36,093
Come on, Mi-young.

930
00:56:46,436 --> 00:56:48,538
It's starting to bleed.

931
00:56:56,546 --> 00:56:58,081
Dad.

932
00:57:22,506 --> 00:57:24,508
LEE HYEON-SEOK PIANO RECITAL

933
00:57:26,343 --> 00:57:28,545
Min-ho, come eat.

934
00:57:28,612 --> 00:57:30,914
Okay, Mom.

935
00:57:37,854 --> 00:57:39,823
What were you doing in there, Min-ho?

936
00:57:39,890 --> 00:57:42,759
Huh? I was doing my homework.

937
00:57:42,826 --> 00:57:45,162
Really? Wash your hands so we can eat.

938
00:57:45,829 --> 00:57:47,331
-Okay, Mom.
-All right.

939
00:57:49,833 --> 00:57:53,303
Hey, kid, why have you been
grinning to yourself like that?

940
00:57:53,370 --> 00:57:54,871
My revenge was a success.

941
00:57:54,938 --> 00:57:58,809
I paid Sun-bun back in one fell swoop
for everything she did to me.

942
00:57:58,875 --> 00:58:03,246
Gosh, kid, you must be thrilled.

943
00:58:03,313 --> 00:58:06,783
Hey, Min-gi, why the sour face again?

944
00:58:06,850 --> 00:58:08,952
It's nothing.

945
00:58:12,589 --> 00:58:14,758
-Hey, hey, hey!
-What?

946
00:58:14,825 --> 00:58:16,293
We got an applicant!

947
00:58:16,360 --> 00:58:18,028
-Really?
-Yes.

948
00:58:18,095 --> 00:58:20,464
-Show me.
-Rural Experience Village's first!

949
00:58:20,530 --> 00:58:22,699
It's true, oh my goodness!

950
00:58:22,766 --> 00:58:24,534
EXPERIENCE APPLICATION BOARD

951
00:58:24,601 --> 00:58:25,836
This is amazing.

952
00:58:25,902 --> 00:58:28,538
It's all thanks to
the website I made, right?

953
00:58:28,605 --> 00:58:30,540
Well, aren't you something?

954
00:58:30,607 --> 00:58:34,277
Good job! I'm so proud of our Hyeok!

955
00:58:36,246 --> 00:58:38,915
-You're leaving without eating?
-I have no appetite.

956
00:58:41,385 --> 00:58:44,087
Let's eat already. I'm starving.

957
00:58:47,824 --> 00:58:49,092
Wow… this is for real.

958
00:58:49,159 --> 00:58:51,261
-People are signing up!
-Yes.

959
00:58:54,831 --> 00:58:57,434
Oh no, what do we do about this now?

960
00:58:57,501 --> 00:59:00,504
We're ruined!
I told you guys to harvest early!

961
00:59:00,570 --> 00:59:01,938
What do we do?

962
00:59:03,040 --> 00:59:05,342
Sir, what should we do?

963
00:59:05,409 --> 00:59:08,412
Why so scared, boys? Nothing to fear.

964
00:59:08,478 --> 00:59:11,982
You boys just need to drink
rice wine and play Go-Stop.

965
00:59:12,049 --> 00:59:13,383
Got it?

966
00:59:13,984 --> 00:59:15,685
Why? How come?

967
00:59:15,752 --> 00:59:17,521
This is called winter cabbage.

968
00:59:17,587 --> 00:59:19,623
-Winter cabbage.
-Winter cabbage?

969
00:59:19,689 --> 00:59:22,426
What's "winter cabbage"?
It survives the winter!

970
00:59:22,492 --> 00:59:23,994
Wait for the snow to melt.

971
00:59:24,061 --> 00:59:26,696
You boys just drink rice wine, got it?

972
00:59:26,763 --> 00:59:28,965
I'll go have rice wine… Play Go-Stop?

973
00:59:29,032 --> 00:59:30,634
One, two, go! Let's go!

974
00:59:30,700 --> 00:59:32,035
-It's on me.
-Sir!

975
00:59:32,102 --> 00:59:33,336
It'll be fine, right?

976
00:59:34,137 --> 00:59:36,206
Why do you care about me? Why?

977
00:59:36,273 --> 00:59:37,441
I don't know either.

978
00:59:37,507 --> 00:59:40,644
Why I care about your every
expression, look, and tone,

979
00:59:40,710 --> 00:59:41,912
I have no idea either.

980
00:59:41,978 --> 00:59:44,181
But how can I help caring about you?

981
00:59:45,015 --> 00:59:47,584
You make me feel miserable to the end.

982
00:59:47,651 --> 00:59:48,985
What? What did I do?

983
00:59:49,052 --> 00:59:52,055
The reason you care about me,

984
00:59:52,122 --> 00:59:54,291
a single mom and the Village Head,

985
00:59:54,357 --> 00:59:57,360
is just pity and sympathy
for your old first love.

986
00:59:58,128 --> 01:00:00,897
-What?
-But I really don't want

987
01:00:00,964 --> 01:00:03,900
that kind of pity at all.

988
01:00:03,967 --> 01:00:05,635
So I'll say it one more time,

989
01:00:05,702 --> 01:00:09,873
stop caring about my tone,
my look, and my expressions.

990
01:00:10,474 --> 01:00:12,943
Because it really offends me.

991
01:00:18,281 --> 01:00:20,383
What? Why are you like this again?

992
01:00:20,450 --> 01:00:22,652
Did you fight with Yun-hui again?

993
01:00:23,286 --> 01:00:25,789
Why fight with a woman
who means nothing to me?

994
01:00:25,856 --> 01:00:28,758
Oh, please. You definitely fought.

995
01:00:28,825 --> 01:00:30,727
Sir, wait for me!

996
01:00:33,830 --> 01:00:35,298
Hey.

997
01:00:36,066 --> 01:00:39,202
Let's harvest the cabbages
and ditch this miserable town.

998
01:00:39,269 --> 01:00:40,637
I'm so sick of this.

999
01:00:40,704 --> 01:00:43,240
Once cabbage prices soar,
we can't stay anyway.

1000
01:00:43,306 --> 01:00:46,042
Just hang in there! Seriously!

1001
01:00:47,944 --> 01:00:49,613
Where did Hotteok go?

1002
01:00:52,415 --> 01:00:53,683
Hey, Hotteok!

1003
01:00:53,750 --> 01:00:56,386
What are you doing there, you punk?

1004
01:00:56,453 --> 01:00:58,555
I just bathed you yesterday, darn it.

1005
01:00:58,622 --> 01:00:59,890
Come over here, hurry!

1006
01:00:59,956 --> 01:01:03,026
You're too white, I can't find you!

1007
01:01:03,827 --> 01:01:05,095
Hey!

1008
01:01:05,162 --> 01:01:07,497
You little punk! Hotteok!

1009
01:01:08,131 --> 01:01:09,499
Hotteok!

1010
01:01:09,566 --> 01:01:13,003
Seriously, you'll get all dirty.

1011
01:01:13,069 --> 01:01:14,404
Hotteok.

1012
01:01:15,672 --> 01:01:17,574
Stay right there.

1013
01:01:26,650 --> 01:01:29,452
Hey, is now the time to read comics?

1014
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:30,987
So what?

1015
01:01:31,054 --> 01:01:34,024
Then should I just stare
at an unconscious guy all day?

1016
01:01:38,461 --> 01:01:40,497
-Watch him closely.
-I'm watching him.

1017
01:01:40,564 --> 01:01:41,631
Darn it.

1018
01:01:42,199 --> 01:01:44,267
I said, watch him closely.

1019
01:01:44,334 --> 01:01:46,570
I'm going to see the Assemblyman.

1020
01:01:50,106 --> 01:01:52,209
That guy is always putting on airs.

1021
01:01:52,275 --> 01:01:54,077
Ugh, he's so obnoxious.
